---
title: Crockpot Chicken Tinga
description: Tender shredded chicken thighs slow-cooked with fire-roasted tomatoes, chipotle, and Mexican spices into a smoky sauce perfect for tacos and more.
course: main
cuisine: Mexican
servings: 6
time required: 6 hours 45 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 6 hours 10 minutes
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DqTsb9N3cqY
image: https://cdn.apartmenttherapy.info/image/upload/v1711396540/k/Photo/Recipes/2024-03-chicken-tinga/chicken-tinga-095.jpg
tags:
  - mexican
  - slow cooker
  - chicken
  - tacos
---

Dice the @white onion{1} and smash the @garlic{3%cloves} with the side of a knife. Place the onion and garlic in the bottom of a #slow cooker{}.

Pour the @fire-roasted diced tomatoes{14.5%oz} over the aromatics, then lay the @bone-in skinless chicken thighs{2%lb} on top of the tomato mixture.

Season with @kosher salt{3%tsp}, @black pepper, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, and @Mexican oregano{1%tsp}. Add @chipotle peppers in adobo{2-5}(to taste) and, if you like, optional @chili powder, @smoked paprika, and a @bay leaf{1}.

Cover and cook on low for ~{6%hours} (or high for ~{3%hours}) until the chicken is tender enough to fall apart. (In an Instant Pot, you can pressure cook for as little as ~{15%minutes}; if it has a sear function, brown the chicken and onions first.)

Remove the chicken, let it cool for ~{5-10%minutes}, then shred with two forks.

Discard the bay leaf and blend the remaining liquid smooth with a #hand blender{}.

Return the shredded chicken to the sauce, stir to coat, and set to high for ~{10%minutes} to reduce.

Serve warm in @corn tortillas{} with @avocado{} and @lime{}, or use as a filling for tacos, burritos, quesadillas, enchiladas, or nachos.
